      say: `Here's what Learn gives you. The Create workflow request: a category, a name, flags, a scope, a trigger and the tasks. A changed definition goes to the create new version action. Triggers run on the hire date, the leave date or the creation date, within a hundred and eighty days either way. The pass task takes a lifetime and a one-time-use flag, and Learn recommends at most twenty-four hours for a new hire. And execution limits quarantine a scheduled run, though a workflow's limit isn't in the API.`,
      detail: `Create workflow: POST /identityGovernance/lifecycleWorkflows/workflows with a category, a display name, isEnabled, isSchedulingEnabled, executionConditions (a ruleBasedSubjectSet scope and a trigger) and the tasks; up to 100 workflows in a tenant; Lifecycle Workflows Administrator is the least privileged role. workflow: createNewVersion posts a changed definition to /workflows/{workflowId}/createNewVersion. The time-based trigger takes employeeHireDate, employeeLeaveDateTime or createdDateTime and an offset from -180 to 180 days; the attribute-change trigger takes a list of trigger attributes. The scope's rule may use only the user properties Learn lists, with eq, ne, in and startsWith, including employeeType and the on-premises extension attributes 1 to 15. The Generate Temporary Access Pass and send via email to user's manager task uses the hire date as the pass's start time, takes a lifetime from 10 to 43,200 minutes and a one-time-use flag, needs the manager and the manager's mail, needs the tenant's pass policy enabled, and works only for a user with no other authentication methods, sign-ins or Microsoft Entra role assignments. Learn recommends a 24-hour maximum lifetime for a pass sent to a new hire. Execution limits: tenant-wide or per-workflow limits that quarantine a scheduled run; an updated workflow limit "isn't currently reflected in the API."`,
