      sources: "Sources: Microsoft Learn, Create workflow; Entra ID Governance licensing fundamentals. Chapter 03, “What it leaves to you.”",
      say: `What does Learn leave to you? It gives one request at a time, written by hand. It doesn't keep the definitions where a reviewer approves them, check a definition against its own limits before the request, decide between create and new version, or measure what the workflows achieved. So the kit keeps one file per workflow, lints it, plans create or new version, and counts readiness, each pinned by a test. The verdict: keep Learn's bodies exactly as Learn shapes them, and add the file, lint and plan in front.`,
      detail: `Learn gives one request at a time, written by hand. It doesn't keep the definitions anywhere a reviewer approves them, check a definition against its own limits before the request, decide create versus new version, or measure what the workflows achieved. Each row is pinned by a test in tests/test_joiners_and_access.py. One example body per request: one file per workflow in config/workflows, the v1.0 body plus a _program block the code strips. A scope rule can use any listed property: JW-02 warns on a rule with no coded attribute or one that reads a display value; JW-12 refuses a property Learn doesn't list. Offset and trigger attributes: JW-03 and JW-04. The pass's lifetime, 10 to 43,200 minutes, 24 hours recommended: JW-05, outside the range is a Finding, over 24 hours or reusable a Warn; both of Learn's argument names accepted. 25 tasks per workflow, task IDs in a table: JW-06 and JW-10. 100 workflows on the create page, 50 on the licensing page: JW-07 holds the budget to 50 and refuses more than 100. Execution limits set in the admin center, not in the API: JW-08 needs the limit recorded in _program. A body for a new workflow, a separate action for a version: plan compares each file with the tenant's export; JW-15 warns on a workflow no file defines. plan refuses to run while the files have a Finding. Run history per user: readiness, the readiness rate and what each unready hire lacked. The verdict: keep Learn's request bodies exactly as Learn shapes them, and send them with Learn's cmdlets. Add the file, the lint and the plan in front of the request, and the readiness measure after it.`,
