      say: `The lint has fifteen rules, and each one says where it comes from. Some are Learn's own limits: the category, the offset range, more than twenty-five tasks, more than a hundred workflows, an unknown task I D, or a scope property Learn doesn't list. Some are the program's design: scope by code rather than by a display name, record an execution limit for every scheduled workflow, give access by package rather than group add, and keep delete apart from disable. And the pass rule mixes both: Learn's range is a finding, over twenty-four hours or reusable is a warning.`,
      detail: `JW-01 Finding: a category other than joiner, leaver or mover (Learn). JW-02 Warn: a scope with no coded attribute, or one that reads a display value such as department (design guidance, from Book 03, Chapter 08). JW-03 Finding: an offset outside -180 to 180 days (Learn). JW-04 Finding: a trigger attribute that doesn't fit the category, or an attribute-change trigger on a workflow that isn't a mover (Learn; design guidance). JW-05 Finding; Warn: the pass's lifetime missing or outside 10 to 43,200 minutes (Finding); over 24 hours, or not one-time use (Warn) (Learn; design guidance for one-time use). JW-06 Finding: more than 25 tasks (Learn). JW-07 Finding: more workflows than the budget (50), or than Learn's 100 (Learn). JW-08 Finding: a scheduled workflow with no execution limit recorded (design guidance; Learn says the limit isn't in the API). JW-09 Finding: a joiner that adds the user to groups directly (design guidance, from Book 04, Chapter 09). JW-10 Finding: a task definition ID not in Learn's table (Learn). JW-11 Finding: delete and disable in the same leaver workflow (design guidance, from Book 03, Chapter 08). JW-12 Finding: a scope property Learn doesn't list (Learn). JW-14 Finding: two files with the same display name (design guidance). JW-15 Warn: (plan) a workflow in the tenant that no file defines (design guidance).`,
