      sources: "Sources: Learn, Create workflow; createNewVersion; API overview; built-in tasks; service limits; execution limits; catch-up window; feature availability. Ch. 03.",
      say: `The facts behind the code, read on Learn on November first. Create and create new version share one permission and the Lifecycle Workflows Administrator role, and both are available at L4 and L5. Changes are versions, not in-place updates, and the tenant runs one schedule, every three hours by default. The pass task has a fixed I D and a lifetime range, and its availability in GCC High wasn't confirmed. Execution limits quarantine a scheduled run but not an on-demand one. And a scheduled workflow catches up on a user for three days after the trigger date.`,
      detail: `Create workflow: POST /identityGovernance/lifecycleWorkflows/workflows; LifecycleWorkflows-Workflow.ReadWrite.All; Lifecycle Workflows Administrator; up to 100 workflows; L4 and L5; v1.0. Create a new version: POST /workflows/{workflowId}/createNewVersion; same permission and role; L4 and L5; v1.0. Versions, not in-place updates; one tenant schedule, every 3 hours by default, 1 to 24. Time-based trigger: employeeHireDate, employeeLeaveDateTime, createdDateTime; offset -180 to 180. Attribute-change trigger: triggerAttributes, each with a name. Scope rule: listed user properties, including employeeType and extensionAttribute1 to 15; eq, ne, in, startsWith. Pass task: 1b555e50-7f65-41d5-b514-5894a026d10d; lifetime 10 to 43,200 minutes; one-time use; manager and manager's mail; no other methods, sign-ins or role assignments; not confirmed for GCC High; GA. Pass for a new hire: 24-hour maximum recommended. Other task IDs the files use: request user access package assignment, disable, revoke all refresh tokens, delete user, remove access package assignment. Tasks per workflow: 25. Execution limits: tenant or per workflow, percentage or count, quarantine on a scheduled run; on-demand runs aren't limited; a workflow limit "isn't currently reflected in the API." Catch-up window: a scheduled workflow processes a user up to three days after the trigger date. List userProcessingResults: LifecycleWorkflows-Reports.Read.All; L4 and L5. List access package assignments: EntitlementManagement.Read.All. Lifecycle Workflows and entitlement management: available in Azure Government; Entra ID Governance in the US Government clouds; GCC uses the commercial service.`,
