      say: `Learn's own pages disagree in four places, recorded so a later edit doesn't loosen the code. The pass's lifetime argument has two names, and the lint reads either. The custom task extension has two I Ds. The mover category appears in an example but not in the property table. And the workflow ceiling is a hundred on two pages and fifty on another, so the budget is fifty. Still open: the trigger name for an extension attribute, the execution limit the API doesn't carry, and the pass's availability in GCC High.`,
      detail: `Places where Learn's pages differ, recorded so a later edit doesn't loosen the code. The pass's lifetime argument: Learn's built-in task table names it tapLifetimeInMinutes; the example under it uses tapLifetimeMinutes. JW-05 reads either; which one the service accepts is confirmed in Lab 2. The custom task extension's ID: the same page gives 4262b724-8dba-4fad-afc3-43fcbb497a0e in its summary table and d79d1fcc-16be-490c-a865-f4533b1639ee in the task's own section. The lint knows the first, which Book 19, Chapter 05 also uses; none of this chapter's files carries the task. The mover category: the create page's property table lists joiner and leaver, while its third example creates a mover workflow; the program's mover file follows the example; Lab 2 confirms it. The workflow ceiling: the create page and the service limits page say 100; the licensing page says 50. The budget is 50. What couldn't be verified: the name a mover's attributeChangeTrigger takes for an extension attribute (the file uses the scope's form, onPremisesExtensionAttributes/extensionAttribute10; Learn's trigger page gives no example), and the execution limit, which the code can only record because the API doesn't carry it. Which cloud: the tools read Microsoft Graph, chosen by --cloud with no default (graph.microsoft.com for GCC, graph.microsoft.us for GCC High, and the higher cloud's own endpoint). Learn's Azure Government table has no row for Temporary Access Pass, so its availability in GCC High wasn't confirmed.`,
