      detail: `Audience: developers who build the project's lifecycle automation, identity engineers who own the workflows, and the reviewers who approve them. You should read Python and JSON. You don't need a tenant until Lab 2. Lab 2: register a reader app with a certificate and grant LifecycleWorkflows-Workflow.Read.All with admin consent; as a Lifecycle Workflows Administrator, with Graph PowerShell, send a create or a new version, signing in with -Scopes LifecycleWorkflows-Workflow.ReadWrite.All; set the execution limit in the admin center under the workflow's Settings. Checklist: the reader app holds only LifecycleWorkflows-Workflow.Read.All for planning, and the readiness reads hold only the four permissions in Lab 1.`,
