      say: `Lab 2 uses a test tenant, never production; the authors haven't run it. Export the workflows with a reader app. Make one example edit, moving the pre-hire trigger from seven days to five, and plan against the export. As a Lifecycle Workflows Administrator, send that one change with Graph PowerShell, scheduling off. Set the execution limit in the admin center, and read it back with the validation kit. Check the pass policy and the manager's mailbox, then measure readiness on the start date. Finally, back it out: remove what you created, or send the previous body as a further version.`,
      detail: `Not run by the authors. Use a test tenant in the worldwide or GCC cloud with Microsoft Entra ID Governance trial or test licenses, never production, and test users whose hire date is a few days away. 1 Export: register a reader app with a certificate and grant LifecycleWorkflows-Workflow.Read.All with admin consent; put a token in HRLC_GRAPH_TOKEN; python python/graph_export.py --task joiner-plan --cloud gcc --out exports/joiner. 2 Plan: the example edit moves the pre-hire workflow's trigger from seven days before the hire date to five; plan config/workflows --current exports/joiner/workflows.json; review plan.json and the bodies. 3 Send one change: Connect-MgGraph -Environment Global -Scopes LifecycleWorkflows-Workflow.ReadWrite.All, then New-MgIdentityGovernanceLifecycleWorkflow for a create or New-MgIdentityGovernanceLifecycleWorkflowNewVersion for a new version. Leave scheduling off until the next step is done. 4 Set the execution limit in the admin center under the workflow's Settings, with the value from _program.executionLimit; read it back with the validation kit's VK-HR-06. 5 Check the pass: confirm the tenant's Temporary Access Pass policy allows the file's lifetime and one-time use; run the pre-hire workflow on demand for one test user with no methods; confirm the manager's mailbox receives the pass. 6 Measure: on the test hire's start date, export the users, the pre-hire results and the onboarding assignments, and run readiness. 7 Back it out: Remove-MgIdentityGovernanceLifecycleWorkflow (it can be restored for 30 days); for a new version, put the file back, export again, plan, and send the previous body as a further version. Remove the reader app, its permission and certificate, and delete exports and out/ch03.`,
