      sources: "Sources: Chapter 03, “Checklist,” “Continue the book.”",
      say: `Here's what done looks like. Every workflow in the tenant has a file, and the last plan showed no unknown workflows. The lint is clean against a budget of fifty. Every execution limit matches its file, and the validation kit agrees. The pass is one-time and lasts at most twenty-four hours. Each change reached the tenant as a reviewed body with its hash recorded. The readers hold only read permissions. And the readiness rate is reported for every start date. Next, Chapter 4: access from attributes, and the mover's residual review. Thanks for watching.`,
      detail: `Checklist: every workflow in the tenant has a file in config/workflows, and the last plan showed no JW-15. The lint is clean with --budget 50. Every scheduled workflow's execution limit in the admin center matches _program.executionLimit, and VK-HR-06 agrees. The pass is one-time, at most 24 hours, and within the tenant's pass policy. Each change reached the tenant as the reviewed body in a plan whose manifest hash is recorded. The reader app holds only LifecycleWorkflows-Workflow.Read.All for planning, and the readiness reads hold only the four permissions in Lab 1. The day-one readiness rate is reported for each start date against the approved threshold. Next: Chapter 04 — Access from Attributes and the Mover's Residual Review.`,
